<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Connemara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Connemara is a region of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-galway">County Galway</a>, Ireland, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-corrib">Lough Corrib</a> and the Atlantic. A land of bogs, lakes and mountains such as the Twelve Bens, it was ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oflaherty">O'Flaherty</a> lords of Iar Connacht in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. It holds one of the largest Irish-speaking areas in the country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/connemara.jpg" alt="Connemara" width="320" height="286" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Own work · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Connemara_and_Joyce_country.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
